e action a second time, save, and verify the same invariants plus no duplicate managed tracks/items; only prior tracks recorded in the sidecar and still `[vgt]`-prefixed may be removed.\\012- Record the command/procedure and results in the repository so Phase 0 can be independently verified in the installed-REAPER environment.\\012\\012Ground rules:\\012- Do real, incremental work toward closing this issue.\\012- Commit your work with git as you go.\\012- You are working on branch `issue-4-verify-phase-0-apply-against-a-live-reap`. Your working directory is `/Users/marekkucharski/projects/.pm-worktrees/vgt/issue-4`.\\012Commit your work to this branch as you go. Do NOT push to main or merge to main.\\012When the implementation is complete and tests pass, push the branch:\\012  git push origin issue-4-verify-phase-0-apply-against-a-live-reap\\012Then mark the issue ready for review:\\012    gh issue edit 4 --repo mrkkucharski/vgt --add-label status:ready-for-review --remove-label status:working\\012  A separate reviewer agent will then inspect your work and either accept it (closing\\012  the issue) or request fixes.\\012- If you get blocked (missing decision, credentials, external dependency): add the\\012  `status:blocked` label AND remove `status:working`:\\012    gh issue edit 4 --repo mrkkucharski/vgt --add-label status:blocked --remove-label status:working\\012  leave a comment explaining why, and stop.\\012- Do NOT set `status:blocked` because the issue has sub-tasks -- the orchestrator\\012  handles sub-task ordering automatically via GitHub's native sub-issue relationships.\\012  Only use `status:blocked` when you need a human decision or external resource that\\012  you cannot obtain yourself.\\012- If you run out of meaningful work to do this turn but the issue isn't finished, just\\012  stop naturally -- you'll be resumed later.\\012- Priority labels (`priority:high`, `priority:medium`, `priority:neutral`, `priority:low`,\\012  `priority:optional`) are already set on this issue by the project owner. If you\\012  create any new GitHub issues (sub-tasks, follow-ups), always include a priority label.\\012- Do not touch other issues.\\012 --json\n89686 /bin/zsh -c ps -ax -o pid=,command= | rg -i '[R]EAPER' || true; ls -la \"$HOME/Library/Application Support/REAPER\" | sed -n '1,120p'; find \"$HOME/Library/Application Support/REAPER\" -maxdepth 2 -type f -iname '*action*' -o -iname '*kb*' | sed -n '1,120p'; git show origin/main:README.md | sed -n '1,30p'\ntotal 136\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 23 marekkucharski  staff    736 Jul 18 09:42 .\ndrwx------+ 56 marekkucharski  staff   1792 Jul 18 09:38 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@  4 marekkucharski  staff    128 Jul 18 09:38 ColorThemes\ndrwxr-xr-x@  2 marekkucharski  staff     64 Jul 18 09:38 Cursors\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 12 marekkucharski  staff    384 Jul 18 09:38 Data\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 24 marekkucharski  staff    768 Jul 18 09:38 Effects\ndrwxr-xr-x@  4 marekkucharski  staff    128 Jul 18 09:38 KeyMaps\ndrwxr-xr-x@  2 marekkucharski  staff     64 Jul 18 09:38 LangPack\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 marekkucharski  staff     96 Jul 18 09:38 MIDINoteNames\ndrwxr-xr-x@  2 marekkucharski  staff     64 Jul 18 09:38 MouseMaps\ndrwxr-xr-x@  5 marekkucharski  staff    160 Jul 18 09:38 OSC\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 marekkucharski  staff     96 Jul 18 09:38 Scripts\ndrwxr-xr-x@  2 marekkucharski  staff     64 Jul 18 09:38 UserPlugins\n-rw-r--r--@  1 marekkucharski  staff   1265 Jul 18 09:38 reaper-fxtags.ini\n-rw-r--r--@  1 marekkucharski  staff      5 Jul 18 09:38 reaper-install-rev.txt\n-rw-r--r--@  1 marekkucharski  staff  34092 Jul 18 09:38 reaper-jsfx.ini\n-rw-r--r--@  1 marekkucharski  staff    377 Jul 18 09:39 reaper-license.rk\n-rw-r--r--@  1 marekkucharski  staff      0 Jul 18 09:38 reaper-midihw.ini\n-rw-r--r--@  1 marekkucharski  staff    516 Jul 18 09:38 reaper-mouse.ini\n-rw-r--r--@  1 marekkucharski  staff     93 Jul 18 09:38 reaper-reginfo2.ini\n-rw-r--r--@  1 marekkucharski  staff   1606 Jul 18 09:38 reaper-vstplugins_arm64.ini\n-rw-r--r--@  1 marekkucharski  staff     28 Jul 18 09:42 reaper-wndpos.ini\n-rw-r--r--@  1 marekkucharski  staff    984 Jul 18 09:42 reaper.ini\n# vgt\n\nPhase 0 of virtual guitar teacher: safe REAPER project plumbing. It reads an RPP project from the command line and uses a REAPER ReaScript action to add a small, vgt-owned practice area.\n\n## Install and inspect\n\nWith Python 3.11 and `uv`:\n\n```sh\nuv tool install .\nvgt \"test/Seven Rivers/Seven Rivers.RPP\"\n```\n\n`vgt [project.rpp]` (or the explicit `vgt inspect [project.rpp]`) accepts an explicit `.RPP` path. Without one it selects the only `.RPP` in the current directory; it refuses to guess if there are zero or multiple projects. It reports the project's sample rate, tempo/time signature, and track names/GUIDs.\n\n## Apply inside REAPER\n\nOpen and save the target project in REAPER 7.x. In **Actions → Show action list → ReaScript: Load**, load [reascript/vgt_phase0_apply.lua](reascript/vgt_phase0_apply.lua), then run it.\n\nThe action is intentionally the mutation path: it uses REAPER's API and never text-edits an RPP. It:\n\n- creates `[vgt] Practice`, a REAPER folder, and its `[vgt] Mirror` child;\n- clones file-backed source media to the mirror track without adding sends, changing source tracks, or changing project tempo/sample rate;\n- writes the adjacent `vgt.json` sidecar with schema version 1, its two created track GUIDs, and minimal config;\n- on re-apply, deletes only tracks whose GUID occurs in `vgt.json` **and** whose current name begins `[vgt]`, then recreates the same area.\n\nThe folder/mirror are therefore idempotent and original tracks remain untouched. REAPER-native click-source items have no file to clone and are deliberately skipped; the fixture's three audio stems are mirrored. `vgt apply` validates the project path and directs you to this action rather than silently falling back to unsafe RPP editing.\n\nUse a copy of any project when experimenting; the included `test/Seven Rivers` fixture is read-mostly.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
